# P4 REVISION v1.x - the Tab5 as it has shipped from the factory so far (M5_CHIP=v1,
# the default). Added to sdkconfig.defaults by the root CMakeLists.txt.
#
# The Tab5's P4 is an engineering sample, a revision BEFORE 3.0. IDF's own
# Kconfig warns: "Revisions higher than 3.0 (included) and revisions less
# than 3.0 have huge hardware difference."
#
# Without these keys IDF assumes rev >= 3.01 and a 400MHz CPU (its default), and the
# BOOTLOADER SECOND STAGE DOES NOT EXECUTE: the ROM loads the segments, jumps
# to the entry, and the very first instruction is illegal (MTVAL=0x0), followed by a
# watchdog reset in an infinite loop. No app log appears at all - it never runs.
#
# The Arduino framework gets this right by itself because the board json declares
# "chip_variant": "esp32p4_es" and it uses the precompiled sdkconfig
# framework-arduinoespressif32-libs/esp32p4_es (REV_MIN_FULL=1, CPU 360MHz).
# With framework = espidf that chip_variant is IGNORED - here we are the ones
# who have to declare it.
CONFIG_ESP32P4_SELECTS_REV_LESS_V3=y
CONFIG_ESP32P4_REV_MIN_1=y
CONFIG_ESP_DEFAULT_CPU_FREQ_MHZ_360=y
